  <running_head>PRO VETERI MEDICINA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">intestini partẽ distendi vidimus. Tur-</l>
    <l n="2">gebat igitur intestinum in præmissis</l>
    <l n="3">quibus experimentis propter materiæ</l>
    <l n="4">ive humorum in eo contentorum, bi-</l>
    <l n="5">is videlicet &amp; succi pancreatici, præ-</l>
    <l n="6">ertim orgasmum: atque hinc consta-</l>
    <l n="7">bat veritas comparationis Galeni, qua</l>
    <l n="8">Comment. in I. Sect. Aphor. 22. &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">in IV. Aphor.10. ὀεγᾶν explicat. Quod</l>
    <l n="10">it Metaphora ab animantibus conci-</l>
    <l n="11">atis in Venerem translata ad humo-</l>
    <l n="12">es: uti enim animalia libidine incen-</l>
    <l n="13">a moventur ad feminis excretionem,</l>
    <l n="14">imò &amp; eorum genitalia turgent) sic</l>
    <l n="15">&amp; humores, dum motu feruntur con-</l>
    <l n="16">citatiore hominibus sunt molesti, &amp;</l>
    <l n="17">loca quæ occupant distendunt. Oculis</l>
    <l n="18">insuper offerebatur quid esset μετεωρί-</l>
    <l n="19">ζεσθαι effervescere, quod vulgò vertitur</l>
    <l n="20">in sublime attolli, agitatis &amp; distractis</l>
    <l n="21">illis humorum particulis, acidis, sal-</l>
    <l n="22">is &amp; amaris, sive contrariis qualitati-</l>
    <l n="23">bus sive facultatibus in sese mutuò</l>
    <l n="24">agentibus: Multò enim altior evade-</l>
    <l n="25">bat</l>
    <l n="26" type="foot" para="true">Comment. in I. Sect. Aphor. 22. &amp; in IV. Aphor. 10.</l>
  </main_text>
